{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/119888-gmc-rules-and-memorabilia-need-for-a-nerf","id":119888,"title":"GMC rules and Memorabilia, need for a nerf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-26T12:29:11-07:00","id":119888,"title":"GMC rules and Memorabilia, need for a nerf?","content":"So If I'm reading the updated rules in GMC correctly, weapons now deal automatic damage if your strength/dex + weaponry/firearms attack hits correct? That is all fine and dandy, but my concern is with memorabilia weapons. Lets take an attack that gets a single success, then a weapon with a damage rating of 2, then make it memorabilia giving it an extra 5. That is eight points of lethal damage on the low end. That is sort of frightening. So after I start running a Geist game with the GMC rules in place, I'm probably going to have to house rule that. I considered giving it a lower damage boost, or even giving the attack the rote effect.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T12:56:34-07:00","id":119906,"title":"","content":"I'd just make the +5 bonus dice","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T13:06:34-07:00","id":119917,"title":"","content":"I am using the combat parts of the GMC rules with Balance of Shadows, and I do exactly what The King's Raven suggested. Just keep them as dice to hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T18:48:40-07:00","id":120083,"title":"","content":"I'd say it depends on what you're gunning for. Thematically, Memorabilia are necromantic artifacts infused with deathly energy of hundreds if not thousands of people, and the death and emotion that that entails. So thematically, you could easily justify the +5 automatic damage for weapons. I'm thinking items like the gun which killed Franz Ferdinand, starting World War 1 and World War 2 by proxy. It would make sense, that that weapon has lain in the Underworld, and fed upon the uncountable death it coursed, becoming almost a thematically representation of death and murder, more than a physical object.<br /> Of course this is an extream example, but still. And mechanically, it is something like a 5 dot merit, which isn't inexpensive if bough with XP, and not easy to aquire, if handeled in-game. Additionally, other people might want it and try to steal it or convince/seduce the owner to let go of it. <br /> <br /> Certainly, you could do what The Baron and Raven does, but my own personal preferance is that doing that, takes away the mechanical awe that is suposed to go hand in hand with the thematical awe, of a necromantic artifact of legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T18:41:40-07:00","id":121350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/119888-gmc-rules-and-memorabilia-need-for-a-nerf?p=120083#post120083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it depends on what you're gunning for. Thematically, Memorabilia are necromantic artifacts infused with deathly energy of hundreds if not thousands of people, and the death and emotion that that entails. So thematically, you could easily justify the +5 automatic damage for weapons. I'm thinking items like the gun which killed Franz Ferdinand, starting World War 1 and World War 2 by proxy. It would make sense, that that weapon has lain in the Underworld, and fed upon the uncountable death it coursed, becoming almost a thematically representation of death and murder, more than a physical object.<br /> Of course this is an extream example, but still. And mechanically, it is something like a 5 dot merit, which isn't inexpensive if bough with XP, and not easy to aquire, if handeled in-game. Additionally, other people might want it and try to steal it or convince/seduce the owner to let go of it.<br /> <br /> Certainly, you could do what The Baron and Raven does, but my own personal preferance is that doing that, takes away the mechanical awe that is suposed to go hand in hand with the thematical awe, of a necromantic artifact of legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that working, thematically. But as far as the mechanics goes, it would be too much of an &quot;I win&quot; button to whomever has it. If I did keep it as five auto damage, I would probably then house rule that every attack with it would cost a point of plasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:49:39-07:00","id":139742,"title":"","content":"a quick aside, if i may, but do people find Geist to work well with GMC as-is?<br /> <br /> thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T14:07:39-07:00","id":139771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicodemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/119888-gmc-rules-and-memorabilia-need-for-a-nerf?p=139742#post139742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a quick aside, if i may, but do people find Geist to work well with GMC as-is?<br /> <br /> thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, as in the direct mechanics?<br /> <br /> The ones that treat anchors as discrete objects and ghosts as un-Ranked entities and make more than a little reference back to derangements?<br /> <br /> It's not ideal.<br /> <br /> There's the <i>shape</i> of viable adjustments visible, but so much of the rules Geist added to account for ghosts not having all the systems spirits had made it awkward as all get out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}